  === KEY LEARNINGS (for future missions) ===

  L1. SMALL-SAMPLE PAPER TRADING ARTIFACTS
      F31 (67% funding drag) was a 15-trade artifact in a sideways March market.
      Full 12-month backtest showed funding is only 1.2% of total PnL. NEVER
      build a strategy around a paper trading observation with <50 trades.
      Rule: Minimum 50 trades before treating paper findings as signal.

  L2. OVERLAY EFFECTS ARE PORTFOLIO-COMPOSITION-DEPENDENT
      Partial TP (Sub 3) improved solo s56 Calmar +8.9% but DEGRADED s58 combo
      Calmar -7.8% and s58+s65 Calmar -15.1%. Root cause: freed capital from
      partial close gets redeployed into other strategies at worse times.
      Rule: Always test overlays in multi-portfolio context, not just solo.
      Rule: More strategies in a pool can dilute bad redeployment effects
      (4-edge improved +7.1% where 2-strategy combos degraded).

  L3. HOLD DURATION DETERMINES OVERLAY EFFECTIVENESS
      Time trail improved s65 (avg hold 50h) by +148% Calmar but only +0.2%
      on s63 (avg hold 16h). Fixed TP improved s63 by +17.6% but would hurt
      momentum strategies. Overlays must match the base strategy's time profile.
      Rule: Time-based overlays need avg_hold > 2x no_stop_bars to matter.
      Rule: Fixed TP works for mean-reversion (natural profit cap), not momentum.

  L4. CONSERVATIVE SCHEDULES HAVE ZERO EFFECT
      Time trail schedules starting at 2x no_stop_bars had literally zero
      effect because avg hold is 25h with no_stop=24. Trades exit before
      the overlay even activates. Must start tightening AT no_stop_bars.
      Rule: Start overlay activation at the boundary, not safely past it.

  L5. ENGINE CAPABILITIES ARE REUSABLE EVEN WHEN OVERLAYS FAIL
      Funding exit (Sub 1) was killed, but the engine fields remain for future
      use. Partial TP engine is generic. Time trail schedule is generic.
      New strategies can use these capabilities at zero implementation cost.
      Built capabilities: funding_exit_threshold, time_trail_schedule,
      partial_tp_atr/pct/trail, _partial_close_position().

  L6. CROSS-STRATEGY TOKEN DEDUP IS MANDATORY
      Bug: Two strategies (s63+s65) both entered TRUMP simultaneously in
      4-edge+ptp. The simulator only blocked same-strategy re-entry, not
      cross-strategy. Fixed: v4/simulator.py:567 blocks entry if ANY
      strategy already holds the token.
      Rule: Multi-strategy pools need cross-strategy position checks.

  L7. abs() BUGS IN DIRECTIONAL LOGIC
      Partial TP prototype used abs(close-entry) which triggered on losses.
      Direction-aware checks are essential for any profit-based logic.
      Rule: Never use abs() on PnL calculations. Use direction * (close-entry).

